# QuR Tag local development. The app needs no secrets in the browser: it calls its own
# server functions at /api, which `npm run dev:local` runs against a throwaway database
# (see README.md). Vite forwards /api to QURTAG_API_PROXY.
QURTAG_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:56861

# Show the switched-off features (src/lib/features.ts) for local work only.
# VITE_QURTAG_LABS=1

# Email (server side only, set in Vercel; never a VITE_ variable). Without a key, password
# reset answers "We couldn't send the email right now" and nothing is sent.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# QURTAG_EMAIL_FROM="QuR Tag <no-reply@qurtag.com>"

# ---- Memberships (Plus and Family). Server side only, set in Vercel (Production). Never a VITE_ variable,
# except the one public key named below. Without them the pricing page and the Membership screen show
# "Coming soon" instead of buttons that cannot work.
#
# Stripe (the web). The webhook URL to give Stripe is https://www.qurtag.com/api/fn/stripe-webhook with the
# events checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.created, customer.subscription.updated and
# customer.subscription.deleted.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=            sk_live_... (or sk_test_... to try it)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=        whsec_..., shown when the webhook endpoint is made
# STRIPE_PRICE_PLUS_YEARLY=     price_... ($19 a year, recurring)
# STRIPE_PRICE_FAMILY_YEARLY=   price_... ($29 a year, recurring)
#
# RevenueCat (the iPhone app). The webhook URL to give RevenueCat is https://www.qurtag.com/api/fn/revenuecat-webhook
# and its "Authorization header value" must be exactly this secret.
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH=      any long random string you also paste into RevenueCat's webhook settings
#
# The RevenueCat PUBLIC iOS SDK key (starts with appl_). Public, so it is a build setting for the iPhone app:
# put it in .env.local on the Mac that builds the app, then run `npm run cap:sync`. It is not set in Vercel.
# VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_API_KEY=
